{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681/events","html_url":"https://github.com/symfony/symfony/issues/37681","id":666549496,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2NjY1NDk0OTY=","number":37681,"title":"[DomCrawler] HTML5 not recognized when document starts with a comment","user":{"login":"bert-w","id":10498595,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk4NTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10498595?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w","html_url":"https://github.com/bert-w","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-w/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":100079,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDAwNzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"e10c02","default":false,"description":null},{"id":149840,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDk4NDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/labels/DomCrawler","name":"DomCrawler","color":"DDDDDD","default":false,"description":null},{"id":3113949,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTEzOTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/labels/Good%20first%20issue","name":"Good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":false,"description":"Ideal for your first contribution! (some Symfony experience may be required)"},{"id":844722949,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NDQ3MjI5NDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/labels/Help%20wanted","name":"Help wanted","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issues and PRs which are looking for volunteers to complete them."}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2020-07-27T20:02:07Z","updated_at":"2020-08-12T06:19:14Z","closed_at":"2020-08-12T06:19:14Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Symfony version(s) affected**: 4.4.11 (`symfony/dom-crawler`)\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\nSymfony DOM crawler has an option to use a HTML5 parser when you install the respective package ( `masterminds/html5`). However, this parser is specifically checking for a HTML5 doc-type as the first content in the HTML. The following situation therefore does not work (see reproduction):\r\n\r\n**How to reproduce** \r\nConsider the following file `sample.html`: \r\n```html\r\n<!--\r\n    This is a comment\r\n-->\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<body>\r\n    <h1>Hello</h1>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nNext, we create a crawler with this content:\r\n```php\r\n$crawler = new \\Symfony\\Component\\DomCrawler\\Crawler(file_get_contents('sample.html'), 'https://example.com');\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe file above is now parsed using the regular non-html5 parser.\r\n\r\nAs seen on this line https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/master/src/Symfony/Component/DomCrawler/Crawler.php#L186,\r\nit evaluates to `parseXhtml` instead of the expected `parseHtml5`:\r\n```php\r\n$dom = null !== $this->html5Parser && strspn($content, \" \\t\\r\\n\") === stripos($content, '<!doctype html>') ? $this->parseHtml5($content, $charset) : $this->parseXhtml($content, $charset);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis creates trivial issues since it is actually a HTML5 document.\r\n\r\nP.S. I dont know if the html sample above is according to spec.\r\n\r\n**Possible Solution** \r\n**1)**\r\nA dirty fix I'm using is simply discarding any HTML comments using a regex:\r\n```\r\n$content = preg_replace('/<!--.*?-->/s', '', file_get_contents('sample.html'));\r\n$crawler = new Crawler($content, ...);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is unlikely to be a closing solution. I can imagine there being websites that have `<script>` tags or even other html elements before the `<!DOCTYPE html>` definition. Again, I do not know if this is against html5 spec.\r\n\r\n**2)**\r\nAdd a feature so the HTML5 parser can be forced for any content you pass. I have no clue what implications this has because this causes non-html5 content to be parsed by the HTML5 parser.","closed_by":{"login":"fabpot","id":47313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MzEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot","html_url":"https://github.com/fabpot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fabpot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/issues/37681/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}